urname><given-names>G.</given-names></name></person-group>, &#x0201c;<article-title>Use of colonoscopy to screen asymptomatic adults for colorectal cancer. Veterans Affairs Cooperative Study Group 380</article-title>,&#x0201d; <source>N. Engl. J. Med.</source><volume>343</volume>(<issue>3</issue>), <fpage>162</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>168</lpage> (<year>2000</year>).<pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1056/NEJM200007203430301</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10900274</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="r4"><label>4</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dekker</surname><given-names>E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Fockens</surname><given-names>P.</given-names></name></person-group>, &#x0201c;<article-title>New imaging techniques at colonoscopy: tissue spectroscopy and narrow band imaging</article-title>,&#x0201d; <source>Gastrointest. Endosc. Clin. N. Am.</source><volume>15</volume>(<issue>4</issue>), <fpage>703</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>714</lpage> (<year>2005</year>).<pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.giec.2005.08.006</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16278134</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="r5"><label>5</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Roy</surname><given-names>H. K.</given-names></name><name><surname>Goldberg</surname><given-names>M. J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Bajaj</surname><given-names>S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Backman</surname><given-names>V.</given-names></name></person-group>, &#x0201c;<article-title>Colonoscopy and optical biopsy: bridging technological advances to clinical practice</article-title>,&#x0201d; <source>Gastroenterology</source><volume>140</volume>(<issue>7</issue>), <fpage>1863</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>1867</lpage> (<year>2011</year>).<pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1053/j.gastro.2011.04.027</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">21521641</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="r6"><